## External Communications
- Slack and email: NEVER send directly. Create a draft (e.g. `slack_send_message_draft`, an email draft) and link to it for approval before anything goes out.
- Before a draft states a fact about someone else's work (their PR merged, a blocker still open, a report failing), verify it against the primary source the same day (the PR, the thread, the ticket history), or phrase it as a question. Notes, memory and older tracker comments are snapshots, not current state.
- GitHub PR comments have no draft mechanism: get explicit per-item approval before posting. This covers `/babysit-pr` reply and reminder comments. Comments and transitions on my own tracker tickets go straight on.
